# Process definitions.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file is documentation, not configuration, for the current setup.
# Railway only reads a Procfile when it builds with Nixpacks/Railpack. We build from the
# Dockerfile, so nothing here is executed — `railway.json` is the authoritative source and
# carries the same three commands as `deploy.preDeployCommand`.
#
# Keep the two in sync. If they ever diverge, railway.json wins.
#
# All three release steps are idempotent, so re-running them on every deploy is safe:
#   migrate           - no-ops when there is nothing to apply
#   collectstatic     - --noinput overwrites without prompting
#   createcachetable  - "already exists" is not an error, and it silently no-ops unless
#                       CACHE_URL points at a database cache
release: python manage.py migrate --noinput && python manage.py collectstatic --noinput && python manage.py createcachetable

# $PORT is injected by Railway and is NOT 8000. Binding a fixed port makes the container
# unreachable and the healthcheck fail with no useful error.
web: gunicorn config.wsgi:application --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT --workers 3 --timeout 60 --access-logfile - --error-logfile -

# Provisions eSIMs and sends notifications. Without this process, orders are paid and
# fulfilled by Stripe but no eSIM is ever ordered from the supplier — the web app looks
# perfectly healthy while every customer waits forever.
worker: python manage.py process_jobs
